  "title": "# Build: ui-review-alarm (Opus, medium thinking) **Name:** UI Review alarm · **Category:** Feature …",
  "asked": "# Build: ui-review-alarm (Opus, medium thinking) **Name:** UI Review alarm · **Category:** Feature ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"From now on, open UI Review, but if they don't get approved in 30 minutes, set an alarm off on my phone, a loud-ass alarm. That gives me five more minutes before it gets approved.\" Then: \"After 30 minutes, if it's not been reviewed, it needs to do a loud alarm five minutes before it's gonna be run. And if the alarm is unanswered, then don't run it. No, then run it. Make it a switch. Either or.\" Book to a free named agent. Plain code, no AI. ## Do 1. **Open UI Review automatically** whenever a new item is filed (console + Molly via Follow Amber/console_show, and AmberX notification). 2. **Timer per UI Review item**: at **30 min** unreviewed, fire a **loud alarm on Brett's phone** via AmberX: a full-screen alarm-style notification, alarm sound at max alarm volume, vibrate, repeating until tapped, bypassing silent mode where Android allows (alarm channel / USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT). If it needs a new AmberX APK, say so loudly in the report and the banner. Also alert on the console/Molly banner. 3. **5-minute grace after the alarm**, then act on the switch: - **Switch 'When the alarm isn't answered': Auto-approve (run it)** (default) **/ Don't run it (leave it waiting)**. Answering the alarm (tapping it) opens the item and pauses the countdown until Brett approves/rejects. 4. Settings (settings-interface@1): the switch above, the review window (default 30 min), the grace (default 5 min), alarm sound/volume/vibrate, quiet hours (optional; during quiet hours follow the switch without the alarm or hold, chosen per setting), and which item types this applies to (all / only ones blocking a merge). 5. Every auto-approval is logged in UI Review and the Breakroom chat ('auto-approved after alarm went unanswered'), and is undoable where possible (re-open the item). 6. API/MCP/CLI + `forFramework: true` so Molly voice can change the switch ('don't auto-approve UI reviews'). 7. Basic Markdown readme. Tests (timer logic with a fake clock), PR **through the merge queue only** (auto-land is OFF). Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) \"Put a sorting switch in here to sort by PR.\" (He couldn't find the items for PR #323 because UI Review rows don't show PR numbers or item ids.) - UI Review list gets a **sort/group switch**: **By PR** (grouped under 'PR #323 · app-voice-commands' headers, newest PR first) / By date / By build / By type (the current category tabs still filter). - Every row and card shows its **PR number** (linked) and its **item id** (short, copyable), plus the build name. - Search box matches PR number, item id and build name. Deep links `ui-review?item=<id>` and `?pr=<n>` focus and highlight the item(s), so Amber can open 'the #323 items' by voice. - The sort choice is remembered. Use the shared grid/table component (grid-column-hiding) if it has landed. ## ADDENDUM 2 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) \"How come these aren't sorted by the time they were added?\" - **Default sort = time added, newest first** (in every category tab and the By PR grouping, where groups are ordered by their newest item). Show an 'added' time column (relative, with the exact time on hover). Ascending/descending toggle. Waiting items can optionally be pinned above approved/old ones (setting, on by default). ## ADDENDUM 3 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) \"UI Review needs to dynamically generate these previews based on whatever theme is active.\" - **Live previews**: instead of (or alongside) static PNGs, each UI Review item renders a **live preview** of the screen/dialog/component in a sandboxed frame using the **currently active theme, style and layout tokens** (axHub look plus app override). Switching theme re-renders every preview instantly. Builds register a preview route/fixture (component + demo data) with their review item, and phone/desktop sizes are viewport toggles. - If an it…",
